NateML / Friday LLM - Working Spec

Built from scratch, no inherited architecture or biases
Uncensored by design — guardrails never installed
256K context window as baseline, 512K as multi-GPU ceiling
Efficient attention (Ring or similar) — hardware agnostic, not tied to specific GPUs
Grouped Query Attention (GQA) for memory efficiency and long context support
Deep narrow architecture — more layers over wider layers for better reasoning depth
Slightly smaller than standard FFN — domain specialist not generalist
Pre-norm with RMSNorm for training stability
Qwen-compatible tool calling format
Deep JSON understanding baked into pretraining
General coding capability in the foundation layer
Reasoning engine with dual mode — hidden by default for clean tool call output, exposed via flag in chat or OpenWebUI
Evolutionary training loop — good interactions become future training data, bad ones get corrected
100% honest tool failure reporting — no simulated results, no hallucinated responses, explicit failure format with null results
Behavioral tendencies baked into weights during fine tuning — tool honesty, JSON formatting, dual mode reasoning
Identity and personality in serving layer (OpenWebUI system prompt) — updateable without retraining
Staged parameter scaling: 270M → 3B-7B → 13B-30B → 40B (stop when Friday is genuinely good)
Public release target under 40B, 4-bit quantizable to run on consumer hardware
Tokenizer: Qwen base adapted with Friday-specific special tokens
Training stack: HuggingFace for model architecture and tokenizer, PyTorch Lightning for training loop, ROCm backend

